  "implemented": [
    "SipAdapter consumes the actual Core-reserved candidate ID through a synchronous dormant replacement allocation. The exact protected context binds adapter/preparation incarnation, verified Endpoint/address/device and target principal. There is no ordinary Participant binding, signaling or per-route task at allocation.",
    "The planned SIP Call-ID is available after allocation and before any INVITE, expressly as correlation metadata. Actual dialog and activation receipt match it. Existing retained activation preserves the same attempt and receipt across dropped or repeated waiters.",
    "Only the actual exact-route SIP translator can mint its private signal source. Configured context objects are refused as signal sources. A bounded queue carries opaque Core events captured at actual answer/INFO-DTMF observation, with weak route/context references and no retained host authority reader.",
    "Core pins actual private duplex readiness and answered state at capture. An early digit cannot become a confirmation after later readiness or answer; observation still rechecks current authority, credential, epoch and readiness. Both delayed modes reject old digits and allow a fresh correct confirmation in controlled guarded media fixtures.",
    "Actual loopback SIP tests cover final answer and single-digit INFO capture without media confirmation, late-event refusal, zero-wire cancellation before start, dropped no-answer waits without another Call-ID and Core-driven CANCEL/BYE before adapter drain. The original native call remains audible.",
    "Physical SIP liveness remains distinct from preparation authorization/lifetime. Current-lifetime loss prevents activation/signals while Core can still tear down the exact physical route. Replacement raw legacy stream access is refused pending guarded media integration.",
    "Fresh full native replacement regression retains successful later-generation movement, Observer behavior, independent target authority, current retained-peer stream revisions and exact target retirement. Captured movement projection failure plus pre-adoption target revocation preserves the retained peer without Core replay."
  ],
